§ `Schedule 4 to the Order -- paragraph 1 of Part 1 of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit Regulations (personal allowances)`

-- The heads of each row are listed in parallel, not as "except where". Where two could both be true (a single claimant
-- entitled to main phase employment and support allowance who is also under 25), the Schedule does not say which
-- governs. The rules take the heads in the order the Schedule prints them, first match (fork F-10); in this Schedule
-- that is the same as the higher figure wherever two heads overlap.

§§ `Schedule 4 (1) -- single claimant`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 ('main phase employment and support allowance'): whether the claimant is entitled to it is an input.
-- src:254 | (6) In Part 1 of Schedule 3 (applicable amounts: personal allowances)—
-- src:255 | (a) the sums specified in paragraph 1 shall be as set out in Schedule 4 to this Order; and
@ref art 23(6)(a) (src:254-255)
-- src:582 | | (1) | A single claimant who— | (1) | |
-- src:583 | | | (a) | is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance; | | (a) | £95.55; |
-- src:584 | | | (b) | is aged not less than 25; | | (b) | £95.55; |
-- src:585 | | | (c) | is aged less than 25. | | (c) | £75.65. |
@ref Sch 4 (1) (src:582-585)
GIVEN `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant` `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` `the claimant's age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` THEN 95.55   -- (a)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25 THEN 95.55   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE 75.65   -- (c) aged less than 25

§§ `Schedule 4 (2) -- lone parent`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 ('main phase employment and support allowance'): whether the claimant is entitled to it is an input.
-- src:586 | | (2) | Lone parent who— | (2) | |
-- src:587 | | | (a) | is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance; | | (a) | £95.55; |
-- src:588 | | | (b) | is aged not less than 18; | | (b) | £95.55; |
-- src:589 | | | (c) | is aged less than 18. | | (c) | £75.65. |
@ref Sch 4 (2) (src:586-589)
GIVEN `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 (2): the personal allowance of a lone parent` `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` `the claimant's age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` THEN 95.55   -- (a)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 THEN 95.55   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE 75.65   -- (c) aged less than 18

§§ `Schedule 4 (3) -- couple`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 ('main phase employment and support allowance'): whether the claimant is entitled to it is an input.
-- src:590 | | (3) | Couple where— | (3) | |
-- src:591 | | | (a) | the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance; | | (a) | £150.15; |
-- src:592 | | | (b) | at least one member is aged not less than 18; | | (b) | £150.15; |
-- src:593 | | | (c) | both members are aged less than 18. | | (c) | £114.35. |
@ref Sch 4 (3) (src:590-593)
GIVEN `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's partner's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 (3): the personal allowance of a couple` `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` `the claimant's age` `the claimant's partner's age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant is entitled to main phase employment and support allowance` THEN 150.15   -- (a)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 OR `the claimant's partner's age` AT LEAST 18 THEN 150.15   -- (b) at least one member is aged not less than 18
        OTHERWISE 114.35   -- (c) both members are aged less than 18

