-- out of text: Housing Benefit Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 14(2), (5); Universal Credit Regulations 2013 reg 29: which condition is met, and whether a carer is paid or has a universal credit award with the carer element, are inputs.
@ref Sch 5 (6) (src:600-604)
GIVEN `which condition` IS A `a condition of paragraph 14(2) of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit Regulations`
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 14(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 (6): the severe disability premium` `which condition` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 14(5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which condition`
    WHEN `Housing Benefit paragraph 14(2)(a) condition` THEN 86.05   -- (a)
    WHEN `Housing Benefit paragraph 14(2)(b) condition` THEN
        IF `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 14(5)`
        THEN 86.05    -- (b)(i)
        ELSE 172.10   -- (b)(ii)

