-- src:611 | | | | (ii) | a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage, |
-- src:612 | | | | in respect of whom the conditions specified in paragraph 15 are satisfied; |
@ref Sch 5 (9)(b) (src:607-612)
GIVEN `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 5 (9)(b): the enhanced disability premium for a person who is neither a child or young person nor in a couple` `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` AND `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST 22.00
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Housing Benefit Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 15: whether the conditions are satisfied, and whether the person is a child or in a couple, are inputs.
-- src:607 | | (9) Enhanced disability premium. | (9) | |
-- src:613 | | | | (c) | £31.40 where the claimant is a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage and the conditions specified in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage. |
@ref Sch 5 (9)(c) (src:607-613)
GIVEN `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 5 (9)(c): the enhanced disability premium for a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` AND `the conditions in paragraph 15 are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage`
    THEN JUST 31.40
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 6 to the Order -- paragraph 1 of Part 1 of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations (personal allowances)`

-- The text prints rows (1)(b), (1)(c), (2)(b), (2)(c), (4) and (5); rows (1)(a), (2)(a) and (3) are not printed
-- (fork F-07). A claimant the printed rows do not reach gets NOTHING; what the missing rows would give is not guessed.
-- The date a member attained pensionable age is an input; a member who has not attained it is not in a printed row.

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether the member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
GIVEN `the member has attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the member attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `the member has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the member attained pensionable age` MEANS
    `the member has attained pensionable age` AND `the date on which the member attained pensionable age` LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether the member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
GIVEN `the member has attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the member attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `the member has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the member attained pensionable age` MEANS
    `the member has attained pensionable age` AND (NOT (`the date on which the member attained pensionable age` LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)))

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether each member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
-- src:301 | (6) In Part 1 of Schedule 3 (applicable amounts: personal allowances)—
-- src:302 | (a) the sums specified in paragraph 1 shall be as set out in Schedule 6 to this Order; and
@ref art 24(6)(a) (src:301-302)
-- src:617 | | (1) Single claimant or lone parent— | (1) |
-- src:618 | | (b) | who has attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021. | (b) | £256.00. |
-- src:619 | | (c) | who has attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021. | (c) | £238.00. |
@ref Sch 6 (1) (src:617-619)
GIVEN `the claimant has attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 6 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant or lone parent` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` THEN JUST 256.00   -- (b)
        IF `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` THEN JUST 238.00   -- (c)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether each member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
-- src:620 | | (2) Couple— | (2) |
-- src:621 | | (b) | one member or both members who have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021. | (b) | £383.35. |
-- src:622 | | (c) | both members who have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021. | (c) | £363.25. |
@ref Sch 6 (2) (src:620-622)
GIVEN `the claimant has attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the claimant's partner has attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the claimant's partner attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 6 (2): the personal allowance of a couple` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age` `the claimant's partner has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant's partner attained pensionable age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age`
           OR `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `the claimant's partner has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant's partner attained pensionable age`
        THEN JUST 383.35   -- (b) one member or both members who have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021
        IF `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `the claimant has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant attained pensionable age`
           AND `Sch 6: the member attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `the claimant's partner has attained pensionable age` `the date on which the claimant's partner attained pensionable age`
        THEN JUST 363.25   -- (c) both members who have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:623 | | (4) If the claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage and one or more members of the marriage have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021— | (4) | |
-- src:624 | | (a) | for the claimant and the other party to the marriage; | (a) | £383.35; |
-- src:625 | | (b) | for each additional spouse who is a member of the same household as the claimant. | (b) | £127.35. |
-- src:626 | | (5) If the claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage and all members of the marriage have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021— | (5) | |
-- src:627 | | (a) | for the claimant and the other party to the marriage; | (a) | £363.25; |
-- src:628 | | (b) | for each additional spouse who is a member of the same household as the claimant. | (b) | £125.25. |
DECLARE `a person in a polygamous marriage to whom Schedule 6 gives an allowance` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant and the other party to the polygamous marriage`
    `an additional spouse who is a member of the same household as the claimant`

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether each member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
@ref Sch 6 (4) (src:623-625)
GIVEN `who` IS A `a person in a polygamous marriage to whom Schedule 6 gives an allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 6 (4): the personal allowance where one or more members of a polygamous marriage attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the claimant and the other party to the polygamous marriage` THEN 383.35   -- (a)
    WHEN `an additional spouse who is a member of the same household as the claimant` THEN 127.35   -- (b)

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether each member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
@ref Sch 6 (5) (src:626-628)
GIVEN `who` IS A `a person in a polygamous marriage to whom Schedule 6 gives an allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 6 (5): the personal allowance where all members of a polygamous marriage attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the claimant and the other party to the polygamous marriage` THEN 363.25   -- (a)
    WHEN `an additional spouse who is a member of the same household as the claimant` THEN 125.25   -- (b)

-- out of text: pensionable age: whether each member has attained it, and the date they did, are inputs.
-- (4) applies where one or more members have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021; (5) where all members have
-- attained it on or after that date. If neither holds, the rows do not reach the marriage.
@ref Sch 6 (4) and (5) (src:623-628)
GIVEN `who` IS A `a person in a polygamous marriage to whom Schedule 6 gives an allowance`
      `one or more members of the marriage have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all members of the marriage have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 6 (4) and (5): the personal allowance in a polygamous marriage` `who` `one or more members of the marriage have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `all members of the marriage have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one or more members of the marriage have attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021`
        THEN JUST (`Sch 6 (4): the personal allowance where one or more members of a polygamous marriage attained pensionable age before 1st April 2021` `who`)
        IF `all members of the marriage have attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021`
        THEN JUST (`Sch 6 (5): the personal allowance where all members of a polygamous marriage attained pensionable age on or after 1st April 2021` `who`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 7 to the Order -- Part 4 of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations (amounts of premiums)`

-- src:632 | | 12.—(1) Severe disability premium— | (1) |
-- src:633 | | (a) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 6(2)(a); | (a) | £86.05; |
-- src:634 | | (b) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 6(2)(b)— | | |
-- src:635 | | (i) | in a case where there is someone in receipt of a carer’s allowance or carer support payment or who has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element under regulation 29 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 or if he or any partner satisfies that condition only by virtue of paragraph 6(7); | (b) | (i) | £86.05; |
-- src:636 | | (ii) | in a case where there is no-one in receipt of such an allowance or payment or such an award of universal credit. | (b) | (ii) | £172.10. |
@ref Sch 7 (1) (src:632-636)
DECLARE `a condition of paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `Housing Benefit (SPC) paragraph 6(2)(a) condition`
    `Housing Benefit (SPC) paragraph 6(2)(b) condition`

-- out of text: Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 6(2), (7); Universal Credit Regulations 2013 reg 29: which condition is met, and whether a carer is paid or has a universal credit award with the carer element, are inputs.
-- src:305 | (8) The sums specified in Part 4 of Schedule 3 (applicable amounts: amounts of premiums specified in Part 3) shall be as set out in Schedule 7 to this Order.
@ref art 24(8) (src:305)
@ref Sch 7 (1) (src:632-636)
GIVEN `which condition` IS A `a condition of paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3 to the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations`
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 6(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 7 (1): the severe disability premium` `which condition` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 6(7)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which condition`
    WHEN `Housing Benefit (SPC) paragraph 6(2)(a) condition` THEN 86.05   -- (a)
    WHEN `Housing Benefit (SPC) paragraph 6(2)(b) condition` THEN
        IF `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or has an award of universal credit which includes the carer element, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 6(7)`
        THEN 86.05    -- (b)(i)
        ELSE 172.10   -- (b)(ii)

-- out of text: Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 7: the number of children and young persons for whom the conditions are satisfied is an input.
-- src:637 | | (2) Enhanced disability premium. | (2) £33.99 in respect of each child or young person in respect of whom the conditions specified in paragraph 7 are satisfied. |
@ref Sch 7 (2) (src:637)
GIVEN `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 7 are satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 7 (2): the enhanced disability premium` `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 7 are satisfied` MEANS
    33.99 TIMES `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 7 are satisfied`

-- out of text: Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 8: the number of children and young persons for whom the condition is satisfied is an input.
