GIVEN `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 8 is satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 7 (3): the disabled child premium` `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 8 is satisfied` MEANS
    84.46 TIMES `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 8 is satisfied`

-- out of text: Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations 2006 Sch 3 para 9: the number of persons who satisfy the condition is an input.
-- src:639 | | (4) Carer premium. | (4) £48.15 in respect of each person who satisfies the condition specified in paragraph 9. |
